  creatureName: Wulong
  description: "The Wulong is a small feathered dinosaur with hooks on the end of
    its wing/arm appendages. This white and navy blue/iridescent dino is about the
    size of an adult human\u2019s hand, feeding mostly on insects. The Wulong has
    been confused for a small species of dragon before, and is sometimes confusingly
    called the \u201Cdancing dragon\u201D due to its elaborate mating dances. These
    dinos have a tail (and tail feathers) that makes up half of their length.\r"
